# rocknix_abl kit provenance

abl_signed-SM8650.elf is NOT committed here - the PKGBUILD fetches it from the
official OpenABL release, pinned by tag + sha512:

  release:  https://github.com/OpenHandheldCollective/OpenABL/releases/tag/v1.1
  asset:    openabl-v1.1.tar.gz (one folder per SoC)
  tarball sha512: edcff09576e3f7c2e0019f526a42df61ddf8ff9867033bbb1ca5c46a71de36b5
                  28986df8950c21b5f53e45e3b12a6de9178815b3120f327b49261aae2cc5c2b0
  (sha256 520cd8fecd26da728259e376561902d9c86b85ad859511066fb1cd4b02b6ab52,
  the same pin ROCKNIX's openabl package.mk carries)
  abl_signed-SM8650.elf sha256 (release's own sidecar, re-checked in prepare()):
                  8fd6a18ec30a8c24751b7db73a6ecb0d9df9f2e1432973273d572841ff3f6216

OpenABL is the Open Handheld Collective's build of the Qualcomm ABL (edk2
LinuxLoader with one patch plus a boot menu, GPL-3.0-or-later; see the
LICENSES.md it ships, installed under /usr/share/licenses). It boots Boot
Loader Spec entries, extlinux, EFI loaders and, what Steamling uses, an
Android boot image at /KERNEL on a FAT partition (board dtb picked from the
dtbs appended to it). One elf serves every SM8650 board; the release keys it
by SoC.

It replaces the ROCKNIX ABL (github.com/ROCKNIX/abl, v1.2), whose repo and
release downloads were removed in October 2026. ROCKNIX switched to OpenABL
in their distribution repo (71d8932b33 "openabl: introduce package", then
a5d0dd4d57 "openabl: bump to v1.1"). epoch=1 because OpenABL's 1.1 sorts
below the ROCKNIX ABL's 1.2.

ROCKNIX renamed the kit folder to openabl/ at the same time. Ours stays
rocknix_abl/ for now: steamling-update-abl keeps its backups in
/flash/rocknix_abl and restore_backup_abl.sh reads rocknix_abl/abl_*.img, so
a rename would strand backups people already made.

The four kit files (README, flash_abl.sh.template, backup_abl.sh,
restore_backup_abl.sh) are VERBATIM copies from the ROCKNIX distribution repo's
old packages/tools/rocknix-abl/sources/ (GPL-2.0 tree). Their openabl/ copies
are the same commands with the folder renamed. Vendored (4 tiny files, change
rarely) rather than fetched or synced; diff them against the ROCKNIX tree
when advancing the sync pin.

Version coupling: the ABL version ROCKNIX pins lives in their
projects/ROCKNIX/packages/tools/openabl/package.mk (PKG_VERSION). Ours (_ablver
in the PKGBUILD) should track it - the ABL defines the boot contract the
profile assumes (FAT label, /KERNEL boot image, board-id dtb select), so a
mismatched pair is the thing to avoid.

The kit's job is FIRST INSTALL from stock Android: the user copies
rocknix_abl/ off the SD's boot FAT to Android internal storage, runs
backup_abl.sh (saves the stock abl_a/abl_b next to the scripts - tell users
to copy those .img backups OFF the device; an install-to-internal later
wipes userdata and the backup with it), then flash_abl.sh, both as root.
restore_backup_abl.sh is the road back to a fully stock device.

Once a device runs steamling, ABL UPDATES no longer need Android: steamling-update-abl
(steamling-bsp-common, reachable from Steamling Tools) flashes this same elf onto
abl_a/abl_b from the running system. It is user-run only - no alpm hook, nothing
at boot or update time, unlike ROCKNIX's updateabl which their bootloader
update.sh calls on every OS update. Its backup goes to /flash/rocknix_abl with
the kit's own filenames and is never overwritten, so a stock backup made the
Android way survives and restore_backup_abl.sh keeps working.
